    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two are base/helper classes). The full suite passes with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to implement the `initials` field:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets an `initials` field.\n\n2. **`PersonNameFormatter`** \u2014 added an `initials(firstName, lastName)` method (with a small private `initial` helper) that upper-cases the first letter of each name and joins them dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"J.S.\"`). This sits alongside the existing `displayName` method since both are person-name formatting concerns.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 wired the new formatter into `toOwnerDto` with a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression, mirroring the existing `displayName` mapping.\n\nThe logic lives in the existing formatter (no duplication), the mapper simply delegates to it, and all tests pass.",
